\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=\\sqrt{5}\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{2}:=\\sqrt{6}\\cdot {R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{5}{2} & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{5}{2}{x}_{3},$ and from the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}.$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=2,$ we obtain the vector \n$x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nNow, we need to normalize $x.$ Notice that $‖x‖=\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{2}^{2}}=\\sqrt{30}.$ So, we normalize $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{‖x‖}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{30}} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{30}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{30}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, an orthonormal basis of ${R}^{3}$ is\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{30}} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{30}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{30}}\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $|{x}_{1}|+|{x}_{2}|+|{x}_{3}|=|-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{30}}|+|-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{30}}|+|\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{30}}|=\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{30}}.$" 13194139535511 true] [17592186352988 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352989 13194139535511 true] [17592186352988 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352990 13194139535511 true] [17592186352988 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352991 13194139535511 true] [17592186352988 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352992 131941395355